design:
This is one user-requested integration sprint: thin Clap metadata generation with two delivery consumers (release installer and static website), inseparable for issue closure. CLI schema is the sole source. The pure sc-composer library does not acquire CLI/website/tooling code or dependencies. No public CLI grammar redesign is needed; share the same command factory with developer tooling rather than cloning parsing structs or creating a second handwritten command list.
Explicit private generator contract (implementation may keep it in a CLI-owned tooling module):
  struct ReferenceArtifacts { markdown: String, html: String }
  fn generate_reference(command: &clap::Command, release_version: &str) -> ReferenceArtifacts;
  fn check_reference(expected: &ReferenceArtifacts, existing_markdown: &str, existing_html: &str) -> Result<(), ReferenceDrift>;
just generate-cli-reference write persists both artifacts; check regenerates in memory/temp fixtures and fails on drift without rewriting tracked outputs. Version comes from the release/workspace version input, not wall-clock time. A release1.8.0 staging invocation must produce the1.8.0 manual/site version; ordinary current-version checks use their actual workspace version. Rust generator/tool entry and any adapter script stay consumer-owned, with no hand-copied schema or arbitrary executable introduced into .sc/sc-lint target descriptors.
U.8 depends on U.7 because it consumes the settled managed aggregate/Justfile/CI contract when wiring the required generated-reference check, avoiding concurrent edits to those same files. It adds no held Clap/serde dependency upgrade; current Clap definitions/APIs are used. Planned output/recipe paths above are part of this sprint's deliverables, not claimed existing commands. Required consumer release manifest changes must be made through the supported sc-publish input/template mechanism and checked for generated parity.
